{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_753604f7f83b0d94d5fdeff1e2a2572d13c6e276b53336223acda03ba53113b5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The architecture is a pure kernel (`createCore()`) providing EventBus, HandlerRegistry, Compositor, multi-backend coordination, and a default cwd handler, with agent, shell, TUI, and providers all loaded as extensions."}],"claim_ids":["clm_753604f7f83b0d94d5fdeff1e2a2572d13c6e276b53336223acda03ba53113b5"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428","id":"pg_1a7bee5c4fe65e7080a59ec1116ecc3d","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/guanyilun-agent-sh-docs-architecture-md-8038ae7730eb-9ec1116ecc3d.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_ee863c2c0bed58b5a9cae73a397c8980"],"title":"guanyilun/agent-sh/docs/architecture.md @ 8038ae7730eb","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_067578336e57aff5da169d9072c7647040d46ad411072e438f50e541efb240a8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Core tools include bash, read_file, write_file, edit_file, grep (via ripgrep), glob, ls, and list_skills; conversation_recall is registered by the rolling-history extension rather than being a core tool."},{"claim_ids":["clm_0f3235d2e61cb0fcd90c541c743035609fc5f0683eb1477a21907406edde1be6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Conversation state is an OpenAI-compatible messages array; ash auto-compacts when estimated prompt tokens cross autoCompactThreshold (default 0.5) of the model's context window, and older turns are evicted to a persistent rolling-history store browsable via conversation_recall."},{"claim_ids":["clm_24353849ad0ed947a8ad3f4840c791e69c33d4cc228fc4d3dae90461387469b5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Tools implement a `ToolDefinition` interface with name, description, JSON Schema input_schema, an execute function with optional streaming onChunk callback, and flags like modifiesFiles, readOnly, and showOutput."},{"claim_ids":["clm_255fef59932579011fbb349995b5c32192b222fe37186815f0789074119438aa"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent runs a tool loop with no hard iteration limit; side-effect-free tools run in parallel via Promise.all while side-effecting tools run sequentially, and results over maxResultBytes (default 100KB) are head+tail truncated."},{"claim_ids":["clm_308942903fd7f609a53ce97e769f5c6d0f4e5f9994ea5876403db915cd756216"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The bundled frontend is a shell on top of node-pty, and the grep tool searches file contents via ripgrep; ash works with any OpenAI-compatible API including built-in providers openrouter, openai, deepseek, ollama, zai-coding-plan, and opencode."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3b0a98f1549298b6ec64e89cb797ebfcfa19117dca8e14c2482e1a2ee22f2fe4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"By default every tool runs without gating ('yolo mode'); the kernel has no permission opinion, and gating extensions can interpose confirmation or policy checks via tool advisors."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5153fe7e95e306e1ea78fea87d7fdc04b96c6cb12bf9b20409fccd6c616e5f20"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Skills follow the Agent Skills standard: directories with a SKILL.md containing YAML frontmatter (required name and description); only metadata enters the system prompt, and the agent loads full content via read_file when needed."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5792c66312ba36d97aaf6feb35e6458f98eac19d66c140ce8970b00519f94949"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The default backend `ash` resolves providers, configures an LlmClient, calls any OpenAI-compatible API directly, and executes tools in a loop until the LLM finishes; it only activates once an apiKey and model are resolved."}],"claim_ids":["clm_067578336e57aff5da169d9072c7647040d46ad411072e438f50e541efb240a8","clm_0f3235d2e61cb0fcd90c541c743035609fc5f0683eb1477a21907406edde1be6","clm_24353849ad0ed947a8ad3f4840c791e69c33d4cc228fc4d3dae90461387469b5","clm_255fef59932579011fbb349995b5c32192b222fe37186815f0789074119438aa","clm_308942903fd7f609a53ce97e769f5c6d0f4e5f9994ea5876403db915cd756216","clm_3b0a98f1549298b6ec64e89cb797ebfcfa19117dca8e14c2482e1a2ee22f2fe4","clm_5153fe7e95e306e1ea78fea87d7fdc04b96c6cb12bf9b20409fccd6c616e5f20","clm_5792c66312ba36d97aaf6feb35e6458f98eac19d66c140ce8970b00519f94949"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428","id":"pg_473b8069080f5aca9ab7f53202fc566d","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/guanyilun-agent-sh-docs-agent-md-8038ae7730eb-f53202fc566d.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_f31d81881f61550b9f2cc60fb4886bf0"],"title":"guanyilun/agent-sh/docs/agent.md @ 8038ae7730eb","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_308942903fd7f609a53ce97e769f5c6d0f4e5f9994ea5876403db915cd756216"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The bundled frontend is a shell on top of node-pty, and the grep tool searches file contents via ripgrep; ash works with any OpenAI-compatible API including built-in providers openrouter, openai, deepseek, ollama, zai-coding-plan, and opencode."},{"claim_ids":["clm_72ec5a38ad78b754541f1918afeae0ce3353e1c2f73dae817cca9e70248b941b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"agent-sh is published as an npm package (`agent-sh`) with a license badge, installable globally via `npm install -g agent-sh`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_761f9deeee81908f0ec6f7fdf178d4bd8daedaa8f19c8e542e1eba3b9e5a6c66"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Native Windows (cmd.exe/PowerShell) is not supported as the host shell; the README recommends running inside WSL for the full interactive experience, while headless/library/ACP-bridge usage may work."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c797267ff84e977963f684ad537fbf8a3b9a0d6a495cfec039f3491ce57f49ef"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The runtime requires Node.js 18+ and supports bash, zsh, and fish as host shells; other shells such as nushell are not yet wired up."}],"claim_ids":["clm_308942903fd7f609a53ce97e769f5c6d0f4e5f9994ea5876403db915cd756216","clm_72ec5a38ad78b754541f1918afeae0ce3353e1c2f73dae817cca9e70248b941b","clm_761f9deeee81908f0ec6f7fdf178d4bd8daedaa8f19c8e542e1eba3b9e5a6c66","clm_c797267ff84e977963f684ad537fbf8a3b9a0d6a495cfec039f3491ce57f49ef"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428","id":"pg_51f8edb5ccbe548f84fd5d4ff3c92e80","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/guanyilun-agent-sh-readme-md-8038ae7730eb-5d4ff3c92e80.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_872821a22f605331bc831be51c1c70db"],"title":"guanyilun/agent-sh/README.md @ 8038ae7730eb","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:52:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e5f2c143cd764917a39945f4e34a6428"}
